Link the INDI client library explicitly in the indi-talon6 build script.

indi-talon6/CMakeLists.txt calls find_package(INDI REQUIRED) without COMPONENTS,
so FindINDI.cmake falls back to its default component set (driver + align): the
executable only records libindidriver.so.2 / libindiAlignmentDriver.so.2 in
DT_NEEDED, while the symbols those libraries import from libindiclient (e.g.
tty_write_string) are resolved at link time through the sibling shared objects
and never recorded.  The musl loader then aborts the driver with
"Error relocating ...: tty_write_string: symbol not found".

Asking for the client component (libindiclient) in addition to the default
driver + align components makes that dependency explicit.  Only the build
script is touched; no compiled source is modified.

--- a/indi-talon6/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/indi-talon6/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 set(INDI_TALON6_VERSION_MAJOR 2)
 set(INDI_TALON6_VERSION_MINOR 0)
 
-find_package(INDI REQUIRED)
+find_package(INDI COMPONENTS driver align client REQUIRED)
 find_package(Nova REQUIRED)
 
 configure_file(${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/config.h.cmake ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/config.h )
